  "note": "Cross-language golden vectors for agent_runtime.contracts.canonical (RFC 8785 JCS). Number rule: a JSON number is allowed when it is exactly representable as an IEEE-754 double (integers above 2**53-1 included, serialized with ECMAScript shortest text); values that would round, overflow the double range, or are non-finite are rejected. Every consumer must reproduce `canonical` and `digest` byte-for-byte. scripts/verify_canonical_vectors.mjs re-derives all of them with an independent Node implementation; tests/test_canonical.py also compares the Python number and string formatters against ECMAScript Number::toString / JSON.stringify on randomized doubles and Unicode strings. Non-ASCII text is stored with \\u escapes so the file is valid UTF-8; utf16-key-order pins UTF-16 code-unit ordering (0, A, a, emoji, U+E000).",
